From c2affa94ed494058a432d6e2ae61e15f17166218 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pleft <elefasgr@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 17:24:53 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] PSP2DC: the memory card kept on the PSP

The adapter still answers the Dreamcast from RAM and writes no flash; the PSP
holds the card as a file. At the start the PSP sends its file (or says it has
none), and only then is the Dreamcast shown a card; every block a game writes
is marked and sent to the PSP, a block a transfer, taking turns with the VMU's
screen. What the adapter holds outlives a PSP that is unplugged.

On the PSP target the USB host is one device and no hub, which frees about
30 KB of RAM (bss 249.7 KB to 219.2 KB). The host driver keeps one set of
buffers and reads a whole card block in one transfer.

Builds; not yet tested on hardware.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
